+ /og_sanitize on   # Enable AI Security Gateway (local proxy)
+ The AI Security Gateway is a **local proxy** (running on `localhost:38790`) that sanitizes sensitive data before sending to YOUR LLM provider:
+ **Important:** The gateway runs locally on your machine and sends sanitized data directly to YOUR LLM provider (Anthropic/OpenAI/Gemini), NOT to OpenGuardrails. See "AI Security Gateway — Local Data Protection" section below for full architecture details.
+ When enabled, all your agents' LLM requests will route through the local gateway for automatic sanitization and restoration.
+ ## AI Security Gateway — Local Data Protection
+ **IMPORTANT: The AI Security Gateway is a LOCAL proxy that runs on YOUR machine, not a cloud service.**
+ ### Architecture & Data Flow
+ Your Agent
+ Your Agent
+     ↓ (LLM request with secrets/PII)
+ Local AI Security Gateway (localhost:38790)
+     ↓ (sanitized: sk-abc123 → <SECRET_TOKEN>)
+ Your LLM Provider (Anthropic/OpenAI/Gemini)
+     ↓ (LLM response with placeholders)
+ Local AI Security Gateway
+     ↓ (restored: <SECRET_TOKEN> → sk-abc123)
+ **Key Points:**
+ 1. **100% Local Processing** — The gateway runs on `localhost:38790` on your machine. It never sends data to OpenGuardrails.com.
+ 2. **Your LLM Provider, Not Ours** — Sanitized data goes directly to YOUR configured LLM provider (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, etc.), NOT to OpenGuardrails.
+ 3. **Local Sanitization & Restoration**:
+    - **Before LLM**: Gateway intercepts requests, replaces secrets/PII with placeholders (`sk-abc123` → `<SECRET_TOKEN>`)
+    - **After LLM**: Gateway intercepts responses, restores original values (`<SECRET_TOKEN>` → `sk-abc123`)
+ 4. **Not Man-in-the-Middle** — This is a LOCAL data protection layer you control. It's equivalent to running a local proxy for security filtering.
+ 5. **Source Code Available** — Full gateway implementation is open source at `gateway/` in the OpenGuardrails repository. You can audit the sanitization and restoration logic.
+ 6. **Your API Keys, Your Control** — The gateway uses YOUR LLM provider API keys (stored in `~/.openguardrails/gateway.json`). OpenGuardrails never sees your LLM provider credentials.
+ ### What Gets Sanitized Locally
+ | Data Type | Before Gateway | After Sanitization |
+ |-----------|----------------|-------------------|
+ | API keys | `sk-abc123...` | `<SECRET_TOKEN>` |
+ | Email | `user@example.com` | `<EMAIL>` |
+ | SSH keys | `-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----...` | `<SSH_PRIVATE_KEY>` |
+ | Credit cards | `1234-5678-9012-3456` | `<CREDIT_CARD>` |
+ | Phone numbers | `+1-555-123-4567` | `<PHONE>` |
+ | SSNs | `123-45-6789` | `<SSN>` |
+ ### Network Behavior Verification
+ **The gateway ONLY communicates with YOUR LLM provider:**
+ # Monitor network traffic when gateway is active
+ sudo tcpdump -i any port 38790
+ sudo tcpdump -i any port 38790
+ # You'll see:
+ # - Incoming: localhost connections from your agent
+ # - Outgoing: HTTPS to api.anthropic.com (or openai.com, etc.)
+ # - NO traffic to openguardrails.com
+ **Verify gateway is local-only:**
+ # Check what's listening on port 38790
+ lsof -i :38790
+ # Output: node (local process), NOT a remote connection
+ # Check gateway config
+ cat ~/.openguardrails/gateway.json
+ # Contains YOUR LLM provider API keys, NOT OpenGuardrails credentials
+ ### Why This Protects You
+ Without the gateway, if you accidentally read a file with API keys, those keys get sent to your LLM provider in plaintext. With the gateway:
+ 1. Keys are sanitized BEFORE leaving your machine
+ 2. LLM sees `<SECRET_TOKEN>` instead of `sk-abc123`
+ 3. LLM response comes back with `<SECRET_TOKEN>`
+ 4. Gateway restores to `sk-abc123` locally
+ 5. Your agent gets the full context, but secrets never left your machine
+ This prevents accidental data leakage to LLM providers during normal operation.
+ **MoltGuard Plugin:**
+ - `moltguard/index.ts` — Plugin entry point, all event hooks and tool call interception
+ - `moltguard/agent/sanitizer.ts` — Local sanitization logic (what data is redacted before cloud transmission to Core)
+ - `moltguard/platform-client/index.ts` — All network calls (only to `openguardrails.com/core` for detection API)
+ - `moltguard/agent/config.ts` — Registration logic (sends only `{ name, description }`)
+ **AI Security Gateway (Local Proxy):**
+ - `gateway/src/index.ts` — Local HTTP proxy server (listens on `localhost:38790`)
+ - `gateway/src/sanitizer.ts` — Sanitization and restoration logic (runs locally, before data leaves your machine)
+ - `gateway/src/providers/` — LLM provider integrations (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini)
+ - **No network calls to OpenGuardrails** — Gateway only communicates with YOUR LLM provider
+ **MoltGuard Plugin (security detection):**
+ | State | Network calls | What is sent | Destination |
+ |-------|---------------|--------------|-------------|
+ **AI Security Gateway (data sanitization — optional, LOCAL ONLY):**
+ | **Enabled (`/og_sanitize on`)** | Proxy LLM requests | Sanitized data (secrets/PII replaced with placeholders) | **YOUR LLM provider** (api.anthropic.com, api.openai.com, etc.) |
+ | **Disabled (default)** | None | N/A | N/A |
+ **Important:** The AI Security Gateway (`localhost:38790`) is a **local process** that only communicates with YOUR LLM provider. It does NOT send data to `openguardrails.com`.
